    "result_text": "The full suite passes (the acceptance suite is the only test in the project). Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nAddress normalization is now applied whenever an owner is created, with the normalized value stored, returned, and used for every address comparison.\n\n**New code**\n\n- `util/AddressNormalizer.java` \u2014 a single-responsibility utility (sibling of the existing `E164PhoneNumber`) that normalizes an address: trim, collapse internal whitespace, upper-case, and expand street-type abbreviations token-wise (`ST`\u2192`STREET`, `RD`\u2192`ROAD`, `AVE`\u2192`AVENUE`). A `null`/blank input normalizes to `\"\"`.\n- `rest/function/owner/NormalizeOwnerAddress.java` \u2014 a pipeline step mirroring the `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`/`NormalizeOwnerEmail` pattern. It binds `@RequestBody` once, normalizes the address in place, and republishes the body via `Out<OwnerFieldsDto>`.\n\n**Wiring**\n\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 `normalizeAddress` is now the first step (`next: validate`). It runs *before* the required-field check so a blank-after-normalization address is rejected, and before `build`/household steps so the normalized value is stored, returned, and compared.\n\n**Changes to existing code (kept small, no catch-all)**\n\n- `ValidateOwnerFields` \u2014 now reads `@Val OwnerFieldsDto` instead of binding `@RequestBody` (that binding moved to the new first step, preserving the \"one `@RequestBody` per pipeline\" rule). Its blank check now sees the normalized address, so `\"   \"` \u2192 `\"\"` \u2192 400.\n- `Households` \u2014 address comparison in `membersOf` and the id in `idFor` now go through `AddressNormalizer.normalize(...)` (reusing the shared logic rather than its old local lowercase-only helper, which was renamed `normalizeName` and retained for last names). This makes duplicate detection and the shared household id both operate on the normalized address form, robust even against non-normalized stored/seed addresses.\n\nThe three acceptance tests (`coreNormalizesWhitespaceAndCase`, `functionalityExpandsAbbreviations`, `errorRejectsBlankAfterNormalize`) pass, and `BUILD SUCCESS` for the full suite.",
